                "entry_id": "e5a493ee-c054-35ce-89ff-c6839a42a9b1",
                "word": "artémisinine",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d121a6fc-dc45-4abe-bb69-eb2507a6afa6",
                        "entry_id": "e5a493ee-c054-35ce-89ff-c6839a42a9b1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "artémisinines"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "802087d8-909b-3f38-bfe8-6c1ba7799314",
                        "entry_id": "e5a493ee-c054-35ce-89ff-c6839a42a9b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Molécule tirée de l’armoise, utilisée dans le cadre de la lutte contre le paludisme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9d9776e-d74c-4251-a7dc-452e38ef51bc",
                                "sense_id": "802087d8-909b-3f38-bfe8-6c1ba7799314",
                                "text": "Un exemple : l'artémisinine, un médicament antipaludique. C'est une molécule naturelle dont la structure a été déterminée en 1979 et qui provient d'une plante, l'armoise."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2d35c51-2b0c-40a6-b82f-aff122e4dbe9",
                                "sense_id": "802087d8-909b-3f38-bfe8-6c1ba7799314",
                                "text": "« L’artémisinine, qui contient un composé chimique unique, le sesquiterpene lactone créé par l'évolution phytochimique, est un vrai cadeau de la médecine chinoise traditionnelle chinoise », a déclaré Youyou Tu, prix Nobel de médecine 2015."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5844769-94fe-4151-a17f-abf53b06d727",
                                "sense_id": "802087d8-909b-3f38-bfe8-6c1ba7799314",
                                "text": "Depuis 15 ans, les accès palustres, plus communément appelés crises de palu (fièvre et transpiration), sont traités par des médicaments contenant un dérivé de l’artémisinine. Or depuis 2008, on constate en Asie du Sud le développement de parasites résistants aux dérivés de l’artémisinine, ce qui pose d’importants problèmes dans la lutte contre cette maladie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "505d3035-88d5-4dfb-b55e-c623b45e1b5b",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5a493ee-c054-35ce-89ff-c6839a42a9b1",
                        "source_sense_id": "802087d8-909b-3f38-bfe8-6c1ba7799314",
                        "target_lang_word": "Artemisinin",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2650a912-4255-469a-bb96-f7f2e4da1760",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5a493ee-c054-35ce-89ff-c6839a42a9b1",
                        "source_sense_id": "802087d8-909b-3f38-bfe8-6c1ba7799314",
                        "target_lang_word": "artemisinin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "artemisinin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb52f3e1-de86-39c8-86ff-a15b5215b925",
                                        "entry_id": "8f0e2f51-13ef-343b-a6f9-50ab071a1faa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An antimalarial drug derived from the sweet wormwood shrub, Artemisia annua, found as the active ingredient in traditional Chinese medical herbal treatment for malaria, chemically a sesquiterpene lactone - C₁₅H₂₂O₅."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f890401-31a5-4a12-8b58-efe346edfca6",
                                                "sense_id": "fb52f3e1-de86-39c8-86ff-a15b5215b925",
                                                "text": "Artemisinin (Qinghaosu) isolated from Artemisia annua is a novel sesquiterpene lactone bearing an unusual endoperoxide function."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1fd0597-2437-4710-86f0-304528d563f2",
                                                "sense_id": "fb52f3e1-de86-39c8-86ff-a15b5215b925",
                                                "text": "The practical value of artemisinin itself as a therapeutic agent has been limited by several factors, however. Artemisinin has a high rate of recrudescence [8], poor oral activity [8], a short half-life in plasma [9], and limited solubility in both water and oil [10]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a380ff31-a3f0-4fa1-a11b-0f72b2435c04",
                                                "sense_id": "fb52f3e1-de86-39c8-86ff-a15b5215b925",
                                                "text": "The emerging resistance to artemisinin is partly due to the complexity of the parasite and the unstoppable nature of its ability to evolve. But it is also the direct result of greed, for which there is no drug or vaccine.\nIn early 2009 the World Health Organization (WHO) announced the discovery of malaria parasites along the Thai-Cambodia border that were proving resistant to commonly used derivatives of artemisinin called artesunate and anthemeter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
